Explanation:
• Field_2 has the highest threat (0.14) and needs 4 drones for full protection. Drone_1 and Drone_3 are very near Field_2, and among the remaining drones Drone_2 and Drone_8 (although a bit further) fill out the requirement.
• Field_3, with the next highest threat (0.10), requires 2 drones. In this case Drone_4 (which is relatively closer to Field_3’s center) and Drone_7 (the next best option) are assigned.
• The two remaining drones (Drone_5 and Drone_6) are left idle since boosting partial protection (on Field_1 or Field_4) would not fully neutralize the threat.
This distribution aims to fully protect the most threatened fields so that the birds are effectively deterred.
